# Sketchpad environment
#
# This app has no required secrets and no backend.
# Leave the variable blank, or do not create a .env file at all, to run in
# local single-user mode: no sign-in, no account, and no auth network calls.
# Boards stay in this browser's IndexedDB under the "local" owner.
#
# Optional Clerk sign-in
# -----------------------
# Set a Clerk publishable key to require sign-in before the editor.
# Use the publishable key from the Clerk application you already share
# across your apps. Sketchpad does not need its own Clerk application.
# Use the publishable key only (pk_test_... or pk_live_...).
# Do not put a Clerk secret key in this file. Sketchpad never reads
# CLERK_SECRET_KEY and does not send board contents to Clerk.
#
# When the key is set, boards are still stored only in IndexedDB, in a
# separate namespace per Clerk user id. They are not uploaded or synced.
#
# Unit tests and the Playwright smoke test force this variable empty so
# they always run in local mode.

VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
